    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a fair point. I'll look into modeling the 99th percentile. But it almost feels like there's something more to it than just bad math. Like, the shipments don't just slow down, they just... stop updating entirely for days, then suddenly reappear. It feels almost intentional sometimes, like there's some hidden factor or little errors in the system that we just can't see. Do you think it's worth trying to hunt down the actual cause of these 'glitches' or should I just stick to the math and increase the buffer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
